integ5 0072 = patches/glue5/0067-glm-greedy-rows-one-launch.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

glm cuda: a window's greedy picks in one launch, and a shared window's in one pick (T3 candidate 1, glue5)

- tf_glm_top1_rows (glm_glue_rows.cuh): block r runs tf_glm_top1's body on row r (rows `ld` apart, words 4 apart),
  so each row's (value, id) words are a per-row launch's bit for bit.
- cuda_engine_pick.greedyRows: one tf_glm_top1_rows launch for the window's rows instead of a tf_glm_top1 launch a
  row; the gather, sync, read and chance.pick per row are unchanged.
- Engine.verifyShared: when no part is structured or sampled (the same on every rank: Engine.structured comes with
  the step's header, a stream's sampling with its begin), every part's rows take one greedyRows call (one launch, one
  gather of world x rows x 16 B, one sync, one read) instead of one per part; each part's rows_at is bound as before.
  Mixed or sampled windows keep the per-part draws.
- Exact: the same tokens from the same words; no arithmetic changes. Collectives per shared round drop from one per
  part to one, on every rank alike (both ranks run this binary).

